<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sŏli</span></b>  (collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Soloe</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Mel. 1, 13, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 27, 22,
			§ 92</span></i>), ōrum, m.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σόλοι</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A town of Cilicia</i>, <i>afterwards
				called</i> Pompeiopolis, now <i>Mezetli</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Leg. 2, 16, 41</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 33,
				20, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">37, 56,
				8</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sŏleus</span></b> , ei, m., =
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σολεύς</span>, <i>of
				Soli</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Milon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					35, 11, 40, § 146</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town of Cyprus</i>, now <i>Solia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 31, 35, § 130</span></i> (Jan.
			Soloe).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
